#. Plugin URI of the plugin
#: metamanager.php
msgid "https://github.com/richardkentgates/metamanager-plugin"
msgstr ""

#. Description of the plugin
#: metamanager.php
msgid "Lossless image compression and standards-compliant metadata embedding (EXIF, IPTC, XMP) via OS-level daemons. Expands the WordPress Media Library with native metadata editing, bulk operations, and a real-time job dashboard."
msgstr ""

#. Author of the plugin
#: metamanager.php
msgid "Richard Kent Gates"
msgstr ""

#. Author URI of the plugin
#: metamanager.php
msgid "https://github.com/richardkentgates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:131
msgid "Site Assistant"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:132
msgid "The assistant acts only through this site's registered abilities. Reads (reports, listings) execute immediately. Writes appear as approval cards: Approve, Decline, or edit the input first. Destructive actions require typing CONFIRM. Every execution is written to the audit trail with actor, ability, input and outcome."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:133
msgid "Rate caps: 50 turns per session, 200 per user per day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:137
msgid "AI provider"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:138
msgid "The model runs through the WordPress AI Client: Settings > Connections holds the providers (Gemini = the google connector; install its provider plugin, ai-provider-for-google) and the API key (option connectors_ai_google_api_key). No provider configured? The assistant says so instead of guessing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:139
msgid "Descriptions derive only from the native excerpt field (enabled for pages and posts)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:148
#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:313
#: includes/metadata/admin/class-mm-metadata-admin.php:267
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:150
msgid "Metamanager Job Dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:151
msgid "This page shows everything Metamanager is doing or has done: pending jobs waiting for the OS daemons, the history of completed and failed jobs, and cron event execution history — all in a single unified view."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:152
msgid "The dashboard refreshes automatically every 5 seconds. You do not need to reload the page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:153
msgid "The dashboard includes three sections: pending jobs, job history (completed/failed), and cron event history with last run times, status icons, and pass/fail counts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:154
msgid "Access to this dashboard and all write operations (bulk actions, re-queue, library scan) requires the Editor role or higher (edit_others_posts capability). Per-attachment actions such as recompressing or saving metadata on a single file respect normal WordPress ownership — Authors can act on their own uploads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:159
#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:161
msgid "Pending Jobs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:162
msgid "Jobs enter the queue when you upload a media file, save metadata fields on an attachment edit screen, run Scan Existing Library from this dashboard, or trigger a bulk or batch action from the Media Library."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:163
msgid "Each job is written as a small JSON file to one of two directories inside wp-content/metamanager-jobs/: compress/ for image compression jobs, and meta/ for metadata embedding jobs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:164
msgid "The OS daemons watch these directories with inotifywait and process jobs immediately — no polling delay. Jobs disappear from this view as soon as a daemon processes them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:169
#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:171
msgid "Job Results"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:172
msgid "After a daemon finishes a job it writes a result JSON to the completed/ or failed/ directory. WP-Cron reads these files every 60 seconds and records them in the database."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:173
msgid "Completed jobs show the file size, dimensions (where applicable), timestamps, and the trigger that created the job (e.g. upload, edit, scan, batch apply, CLI). Failed jobs show a Re-queue button — click it to re-submit the original job file without any manual steps."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:174
msgid "Use the search box to filter by file name, job type, or status. Clear History removes all records from the database but does not affect any media files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:179
msgid "Daemons"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:181
msgid "OS Daemons"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:182
msgid "Two systemd services handle all media file processing:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:184
msgid "lossless JPEG compression via jpegtran; lossless PNG compression via optipng; lossless WebP recompression via cwebp; video container remux via ffmpeg. Files are only replaced if the result is smaller."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:185
msgid "writes metadata via ExifTool in a single pass, using each file's native tag system: EXIF/IPTC/XMP for images; ID3 for MP3; QuickTime atoms for MP4/MOV/M4A; Vorbis comments for OGG/FLAC; XMP-only for AVI/WAV/WMV/WMA/PDF; read-only for MKV/WebM/OGV."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:187
msgid "The banner at the top of the page shows tool availability and daemon health. A green icon means the tool is installed and reachable. A red icon means it is missing or the daemon is not running. Daemon status is read from a PID file — no elevated privileges are needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:188
msgid "The System Status section shows tool availability, the installed daemon version, the version required by the current plugin, and whether they match."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:189
msgid "To restart a daemon from the server:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:196
msgid "Bulk Actions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:198
msgid "Bulk Actions (Media Library)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:200
msgid "Compress Lossless"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:200
msgid "Queues lossless compression for all uncompressed files in the selection. Images: JPEG via jpegtran, PNG via optipng, WebP via cwebp. Video: container remux via ffmpeg. Files are only replaced if the result is smaller."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:201
msgid "Inject Site Info into Metadata"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:201
msgid "Writes Publisher (your site name) and Website (your site URL) into IPTC and XMP. This is neutral provenance — it never sets Creator, Copyright, or Owner."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:206
#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:208
msgid "Metadata Fields"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:209
msgid "Metamanager maps WordPress fields to each file's native tag system. Images write EXIF, IPTC, and XMP simultaneously; MP3 uses ID3; MP4/MOV/M4A use QuickTime atoms; OGG/FLAC use Vorbis comments; AVI/WAV/WMV/WMA and PDF use XMP-only. All field names below apply across all supported types."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:233
msgid "All per-image fields can be stamped across multiple images at once from the Batch Metadata page. Leave any field blank to leave it unchanged on the selected images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:238
msgid "Updates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:240
msgid "Keeping Metamanager Up to Date"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:241
msgid "Metamanager integrates with the WordPress update system. New releases from the apt server appear automatically in Dashboard → Updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:242
msgid "To check immediately, go to Plugins → Installed Plugins and click the \"Check for Updates\" link next to Metamanager."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:243
msgid "Daemon updates are triggered automatically by the plugin after every plugin update. The server's apt channel (test or stable) determines which daemon version is installed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:248
msgid "WP-Cron History"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:250
msgid "WP-Cron History Tracking"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:251
msgid "Metamanager tracks the execution history of all its cron events. Each cron callback is wrapped with MM_Cron_Tracker, which automatically records:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:253
msgid "Last run time and next scheduled time"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:254
msgid "Pass/fail counts (total runs and failures)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:255
msgid "Last 20 runs per hook with timestamps and status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:257
msgid "Tracked cron events:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:259
msgid "Reads completed job results from the daemon output directories and updates the database."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:260
msgid "Writes the status JSON file consumed by GCM and monitoring tools."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:262
msgid "Cron history is visible in the dashboard widget under Metamanager → Dashboard, and in the status JSON file under the \"cron\" key."
msgstr ""

