#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:297
msgid "Metamanager Meta Sync Column"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:298
msgid "The Meta Sync column shows whether file-level metadata (EXIF, IPTC, XMP) has been embedded into the media file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:301
msgid "Embedded"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:301
msgid "Metadata has been written into the file by the daemon."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:302
msgid "A metadata embedding job is pending. The daemon will write WP fields into the file shortly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:303
msgid "Not embedded"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:303
msgid "No metadata has been written to the file yet. Use Embed Metadata from the Bulk Actions menu, or save the attachment to trigger automatic embedding."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:305
msgid "Metadata embedding happens automatically on upload. You can also trigger it manually from the Media Library bulk actions or the attachment edit screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:315
#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:399
msgid "Media Processing"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:316
msgid "This page lets you bulk-edit metadata fields across multiple media files at once. Select files, choose a field, set a value, and apply — the changes are saved to WordPress and queued for daemon embedding into the files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:317
msgid "Fields available for bulk editing: Creator, Copyright, Owner, Headline, Credit, Keywords, Date, City, State, Country, Rating."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:318
msgid "Changes are applied immediately to WordPress post meta. A metadata write-back job is then queued for each affected file so the daemon embeds the new values into EXIF/IPTC/XMP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:326
msgid "REST API Access"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:328
msgid "REST API Access Control"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:329
msgid "These settings control external access to the Metamanager REST endpoints. Logged-in WordPress users are never affected — the Media Library status column and job dashboard always work regardless of what is configured here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:331
#: includes/class-mm-settings.php:273
msgid "Disable REST API"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:331
msgid "Blocks all unauthenticated requests to /wp-json/metamanager/v1/*. Logged-in users are not blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:332
msgid "Allowed IP Addresses"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:332
msgid "Restricts unauthenticated access to requests originating from the listed IPv4 or IPv6 addresses. Leave blank to allow requests from any IP. Logged-in users are not subject to this restriction."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:334
msgid "Normal WordPress authentication (X-WP-Nonce header or cookie) and capability checks still apply to all requests."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:339
#: includes/class-mm-settings.php:289
msgid "Upload Receipts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:341
msgid "Upload Receipt Emails"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:342
msgid "The site admin always receives a batched digest email after uploads — no toggle needed. Each WordPress user can control their own receipt preference from Users → Your Profile → Metamanager → Upload receipts. The checkbox is enabled by default; uncheck it to stop receiving receipts without affecting anyone else."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:343
msgid "Uploads within a 60-second window are grouped into a single email per recipient — no matter how many files are uploaded in that window."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:345
msgid "Extra CC address"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:345
msgid "An additional email address to CC on every upload receipt sent to the admin. Leave blank to send only to the admin address. Per-user receipts are controlled from each user's own profile page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:347
msgid "If an email fails to send, an admin notice banner appears at the top of the dashboard with a one-click retry button. Dismiss it to discard the failed batch without retrying."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:352
#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:354
#: includes/class-mm-settings.php:319
msgid "Data & Uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:355
msgid "By default, Metamanager leaves all data in place when the plugin is deleted — options, post meta, and the job log table are kept so nothing is lost on an accidental uninstall."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:356
msgid "Enable \"Remove all data on uninstall\" only when you are certain you want a clean removal. When this setting is on, deleting the plugin from the Plugins screen will permanently remove all plugin options, all custom post meta, the metamanager_jobs database table, and the job queue directory."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mm-admin.php:357
msgid "The daemon services must be stopped and removed manually from the server."
msgstr ""

